  "body": "Continued from https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/5440.\r\n\r\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/#when-to-obtain-images is referring to a setting user agents can offer to disable images and only load them on-demand. However, it prohibits user agents from offering this setting if scripting is enabled.\r\n\r\nI've tested Chrome and Firefox Mobile (Fennec) and neither follow this spec. Both allow disabling images while leaving scripts enabled.\r\n\r\nI think we should remove this requirement from the spec, via a commit similar to https://github.com/whatwg/html/commit/9eea50399d6b97415ed90c79385ca794005228e8.",
